KG42.register("rules-89e90494b6a870e8451983a5",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R002","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"The ESC, acting as the local market operator, coordinates P2P energy sharing between community customers. Scope: P2P energy sharing between customers within the community Microgrid. P2P sharing permits local buying and selling of energy, including PV sharing among prosumers and trades of surplus PV power with consumers without PV systems. Scope: Neighborhood energy exchanges within the P2P sharing community.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Neighborhood energy exchanges within the P2P sharing community. | P2P energy sharing between customers within the community Microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e007"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESC, acting as the local market operator, coordinates P2P energy sharing between community customers. Scope: P2P energy sharing between customers within the community Microgrid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"P2P sharing permits local buying and selling of energy, including PV sharing among prosumers and trades of surplus PV power with consumers without PV systems. Scope: Neighborhood energy exchanges within the P2P sharing community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems. PP A t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A third party entity named “energy sharing coordinator (ESC)” coordinates between customers and provides P2P sharing services, i.e. assuring the power balance and payment balance [13]. The ESC is the controller of the DERs as well as the local market operator. The ESC is located at the PCC (e.g. the low voltage substation). A smart meter is installed at the PCC, measuring the real-time net power consumption of the community, and this measurement is the input of the ESC. The ESC is communicated with the controllers of these small-scale batteries at the prosumer premises, and provides control signals to them via one-way communication. Through managing the battery charging/discharging, the ESC ensures the maximum use of local energy resources and the minimum amount of electricity fed back into the grid. Therefore the overall energy cost of the community is reduced, and the reduced cost is distributed to individual customers through a P2P pricing mechanism. The ESC also calculates energy bills of individual customers based on the P2P pricing mechanism, using the recorded import/export energy (e.g. half-hourly) from smart meters at the premises."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"g p g time when there is insuﬃcient energy from the PV battery system, the prosumer buys energy from","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing provides options for prosumers to trade energy within the neighborhood through local buying and selling, allowing local funds to remain within the local economy [31]. With P2P energy sharing, several customers in a community Microgrid share the connection to the main grid. The combined load is subject to random coincidence of the individual loads, which averages stochastic fluctuations [32,33]. This means that surplus PV power from a customer can be consumed by another customer with excess consumption.\nFig. 1 shows the architecture of P2P energy sharing. In the P2P sharing community, there are N customers, NB of which have individual PV battery systems installed (NB ⩽ N). Although the PV outputs in a community are likely to be similar due to almost the same solar radiation, the net loads vary between prosumers, because of the differences in load, kWp of PV systems and battery statuses. Therefore, it is possible for the prosumers to share PV power with each other. The surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This rule is a procedural coordination/permission rule in the activation stage. Its supplied source text names the ESC and P2P trading but defines no design-selection or operational decision variable belonging to execution.energy_trade. The paper's optimization variable x_t^i is defined in the separate clearing CNLP lead, not in this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter, constant, coefficient, or bound is introduced for this execution rule by the supplied evidence. Quantities such as N, NB, prices, efficiencies, and battery limits belong to other graph rules/leads and cannot be imported into this rule without changing its scope."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e002","quote":"A third party entity named “energy sharing coordinator (ESC)” coordinates between customers and provides P2P sharing services, i.e. assuring the power balance and payment balance [13]. The ESC is the controller of the DERs as well as the local market operator."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","quote":"P2P energy sharing provides options for prosumers to trade energy within the neighborhood through local buying and selling"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","quote":"Therefore, it is possible for the prosumers to share PV power with each other. The surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"6b06c3d699fb708bb9814a4253aac2ca6fb626aa8fe48c8267fafc81043c3106","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a procedural activation-stage statement: the ESC coordinates P2P energy sharing and local buying/selling is permitted within the community Microgrid. The supplied rule evidence contains no execution-specific equation, optimization variable, parameter, quantifier, or mathematical relation. Mathematical formulations in the paper concern other graph rules/leads such as CNLP clearing, SDR pricing, and settlement, and cannot be moved into this rule. The B evidence remains unreviewed under the experiment policy; this formalization only records the procedural reading supported by the supplied quotations.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the ESC coordination statement that connects the local-operator role to energy-trade execution; it is exactly the constraint attached to the frozen edge from coordination.local_operator to execution.energy_trade."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 describes the permitted local buying and selling behavior at the execution.energy_trade node. C.1 attaches no edge to C002, so no edge is asserted for this constraint."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
